{"type":"event","event":{"type":"thinking_end","text":"Alright, let's read sections 1–3 of the design document and the B2 phase box. I also need to check how the named VM's `:push` is used in linearize's lowering — specifically, where in linearize.cljc `:push` is emitted, and confirm that the stack VM's no-op-ification of `:push` is correct.\n\nMore importantly: the named VM's `:push` commits `val` onto St. In the named VM, value-producing instructions (const, load, closure) store their result in `val`, not in St. `:push` moves val → St. In the stack VM, value-producing instructions conj directly onto the stack. Therefore `:push` becomes a no-op — but only if all value-producing instructions in the stack VM are conj-ing. But wait — what about `:call`? In the named VM, `:call` puts its result into `val`. Then `:push` commits it. In the stack VM, `:call` conj's the result onto the stack. So `:push` after `:call` also becomes a no-op. So what about `:store-put`? In the stack VM it conj's the value. In the named VM, `:store-put` probably puts the value into `val`, and a subsequent `:push` commits it. OK.\n\nBut is there anywhere in the named VM where `:push` is emitted without the immediately preceding producing instruction having been conj-ed? I need to check linearize's lowering to see where `:push` gets emitted. Let's read linearize.cljc.\n\nAnother important point: the stack VM's `:return` pops… actually `:return` peeks the stack and truncates down to stack-base. And `:call` reads operands from the top of the stack. Since `:push` is a no-op and producers directly conj, the stack discipline is preserved.\n\nPotential issue: what if linearize emits `:push` after something like `:branch-false`? I need to read the lowering code.\n\nFurthermore, let's read sections 1–3 of the design document and the B2 box, and additionally check the semantics of `yin.vm.debruijn/resolve-name`, `yin.vm.code/vector-operand-table`, `well-formed-vector?`, `well-formed-image?`, and `scope-defect` to verify the B2 logic.\n\nLet's read these files."}}
{"type":"event","event":{"type":"text_delta","delta":"Now the design"}}
