{"type":"event","event":{"type":"thinking_end","text":"Interesting — the design document hasn't been renamed. The collab brief says \"the design document docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-vm.md was renamed to docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md to match.\" But the file is still at yin.vm.debruijn-vm.md. This is a finding — the rename wasn't actually performed (at least in this worktree, not committed and not staged? git status doesn't show docs as modified). Let me check git status. Actually, git status in the context only shows changes under src/test, nothing under docs. So the document rename is missing. This is P2 (or P1?) — the brief asserts it's done; a review should catch this inconsistency. But wait — maybe the orchestrator just hasn't done it yet. The review should report this: docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md does not exist; the document is still under the old name. Also, the docstrings in the source reference \"docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md\" — pointing at a nonexistent file. This is a stale/forward reference.\n\nHmm, but wait: plan mode is read-only; git status is read-only and fine, though we've been told the snapshot might be stale. Let me run git status to check the current state. Actually, in plan mode state-modifying commands are forbidden; git status is read-only and allowed. Let me check.\n\nAlso, I need to read the document's sections 1–3 and the B2 phase box from the existing yin.vm.debruijn-vm.md.\n\nAlso, check for lingering references to the old namespace name `yin.vm.debruijn-vm` across the whole repo (broken requires). Also read yin.vm.debruijn (resolve-name), yin.vm.code (vector-operand-table, well-formed-vector?), yin.vm.debruijn-code (well-formed-image?, image-defect, image-hash, scope-defect), yin.vm.linearize (lower), and the contract tests."}}
