in code) — but the brief explicitly asks about \"stale docstring references\". These aren't references to old name but they're stale statements. Worth flagging as P3/P2.\n\n- stack.cljc references `yin.vm.debruijn.stack` nowhere as old name. Requires: yin.vm, yin.vm.engine ✓. No old `debruijn-vm` references ✓.\n\n- test/yin/vm/debruijn/stack_test.cljc: ns yin.vm.debruijn.stack-test ✓; requires yin.vm.debruijn.stack ✓, yin.vm.debruijn-vm-contract-test (intentionally non-renamed) ✓. Docstring: \"B2 (the named-datom lowerer) does not exist yet\" — also stale (lines 5-6). P3.\n\n- debruijn_linearize.cljc: requires yin.vm.code, yin.vm.debruijn, yin.vm.linearize ✓ — doesn't require stack VM. Line 147 docstring mentions \"yin.vm.debruijn.stack's :frames\" ✓ new name. No old name ✓.\n\n- debruijn_linearize_test.cljc: requires yin.vm.debruijn.stack ✓.\n\n- debruijn_code.cljc: docstring refers to \"docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md S2\" — but that file doesn't exist (doc wasn't renamed!). Same for stack.cljc, stack_test, linearize, linearize_test, debruijn_vm_contract_test (B0). All refer to docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md but actual file is docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-vm.md. This is the main rename inconsistency: design doc rename wasn't performed. The brief says it was. Finding: P1 or P2? Nothing breaks at runtime (only docstring path references), but the brief explicitly asks to verify rename consistency, and the doc itself (yin.vm.debruijn-vm.md line 282: \"The VM is a new yin.vm.debruijn-vm namespace\", line 389: \"New: src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_vm.cljc\", line 326, line 390, lines 402-403, line 418) still uses old file/namespace names. So: doc rename missing + doc contents stale w.r.t. rename. P2 (must fix before commit? orchestrator claimed done — so P1 against brief's claim? I'll rate P2: it's documentation, no code breaks, but brief asserts a state that's false; commit would ship dangling doc references). Actually all source files' docstrings cite a nonexisten