{"type":"event","event":{"type":"thinking_end","text":"`semantic/load-image` is PUBLIC (line 528). In other words, B2's `named-canonical-vector` claims that the legitimate precedent (`load-image`'s local `canonical`) is \"private to a namespace where only reading is allowed in this phase, hence re-implemented here\" — indeed, the local `canonical` fn inside load-image is private (a local binding), even though load-image itself is public. Since the local helper is unreachable, the re-implementation claim is accurate. However, the tests could also call `load-image` on a named VM and read its `:code`… that would be a more independent structural comparison. At most P3.\n\n`vm/run` — grep found `defn run` only in encoder.cljc. The tests use `(vm/run ...)` and `(v2/run ...)` in stack_test — does `run` exist in yin.vm? Perhaps it's a protocol method IVM/run defined in yin.vm, so `(defn run` wouldn't match a protocol definition. `vm/IVM (run ...)` protocol — called as vm/run. Yes, a protocol function. stack.cljc extends vm/IVM with run ✓. No problem.\n\n`vm/primitives` ✓ (line 159 def).\n\nNext let me also re-check the signature of `ast->datoms-with-root`: the test does `(second (vm/ast->datoms-with-root ast))` — returns [root-id datoms]? Let me quickly check. Line 524. Also verify whether the `:streams` corpus uses the `:val` key — the grammar slot for :stream/put in ast->datoms is [[:target :node] [:val :node]] (line 812) ✓ the test uses :target/:val ✓. :vm/resume slot [[:parked-id :kw] [:val :node]] ✓ the test uses :parked-id/:val ✓.\n\nLet me briefly read the docstring of ast->datoms-with-root to verify.\n\nActually — also check the `:ffi` node in the test: {:type :dao.stream.apply/call, :op :op/echo, :operands [...]} ✓ matches the grammar [[:op :kw] [:operands :nodes]].\n\nAlso `if-in-tail`: `(app (lam '[n] (if-node ...)) (lit 3))` — application lowering: operator :closure, :push, operand :const 3, :push, :call 1 false. Body: test `(app (v '<) (v 'n) (lit 1))` → load-v