{"type":"event","event":{"type":"message_update","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`bind-params` = `(into {} (map vector params (concat args (repeat nil))))`. For params [x x], args [5]: map vector → ([x 5] [x nil]) → into {} — later entries overwrite → {x nil}. So on an under-arity call the NAMED VM returns **nil**! And de Bruijn returns frame [5 nil], position 1 → nil. **Match!**\n\nFull arity [5 6]: {x 5} then {x 6} → 6; de Bruijn [5 6] position 1 → 6 ✓.\n\nSo resolve-name's rightmost-wins exactly mirrors bind-params' last-wins, including nil-padding on under-arity (since map vector pads with nil, the last duplicate gets overwritten with nil). Great — no divergence. The claim in resolve-name's docstring holds precisely because bind-params pads args with nil before zipping (rather than stopping at the shorter zipmap).\n\nPhew. So B2/B3 parity is preserved on this edge case.\n\nNow, are there any tests covering ((fn [x x] x) 5)? None — B2's :duplicate-param fixture doesn't call the lambda. Not a defect per se; parity holds. Could mention as P3: no runtime parity fixture for duplicate-param with an actual call (B5's domain anyway).\n\nAlright, wrapping up the review. Also re-verifying the claim about stack.cljc not requiring debruijn-code: requires are [yin.vm] [yin.vm.engine] ✓.\n\nAlso verified `vm/ast->datoms-with-root` returns [root datoms] — tests use (second ...) as datoms. Line 524 defn. Trusting it; also `lower` internally uses vm/index-datoms to find root via the :yin/root marker. ast->datoms-with-root presumably returns [root-id datoms]. Tests pass orchestrator-run, so fine.\n\nOne more consistency check — test/yin/vm/debruijn_vm_contract_test.cljc is modified (M): what changed? Probably docstring reference to renamed docs. Not in scope for the read list, but part of rename consistency. Its ns is intentionally still yin.vm.debruijn-vm-contract-test ✓, docstring cites docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md (dangling, covered under finding 1).\n\nAlso 