st be honest.\n\nSession-ID: per prompt it's \"pending (caller-generated)\". The scratchpad path contains a session id: 371434a6-5144-4a5f-b739-0af9b69baf07. Use that.\n\nLet me also count what I read: whole files: debruijn_linearize.cljc (388 lines?), debruijn_linearize_test.cljc, debruijn/stack.cljc (266 lines), debruijn/stack_test.cljc (321 lines), docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-vm.md (667 lines), debruijn_code.cljc (852 lines), linearize.cljc (447 lines), plus targeted reads: semantic.cljc (:push opcode 22 + hot loop 180-379), code.cljc (1-413 across 2 reads), debruijn.cljc (590-699), engine.cljc bind-params (46-71), completion.cljc (118-211), vm.cljc gensym/stream-make defaults, plus grep across the repo for old names.\n\nWhat I ran: read_file/grep/glob only; 1 shell_command attempt (git status) which was refused by permissions. No tests, no builds, no edits.\n\nFindings summary:\n\nP1-1: docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md doesn't exist — doc rename never performed. 7 files cite the nonexistent path (src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:2, src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_linearize.cljc:2, src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc:2, test/yin/vm/debruijn/stack_test.cljc:2, test/yin/vm/debruijn_linearize_test.cljc:2, test/yin/vm/debruijn_code_test.cljc:2, test/yin/vm/debruijn_vm_contract_test.cljc:2). Also the old doc still contains old names in its body: line 282 (\"new yin.vm.debruijn-vm namespace\"), lines 389-390 (B3 box file paths), 402-403 (B4 box), 418 (B5 box). Failure scenario: a reader or agent following any docstring citation hits a nonexistent file; repo doc discipline (AGENTS.md → docs/design references) broken at commit time.\n\nP2-1: stack.cljc has stale \"B2 does not yet exist\" claims: ns docstring lines 10-13 and `eval`'s ex-info message (lines 249-251). B2 lands in the same commit; the eval error message asserts something false at runtime. Also stack_test.cljc lines 5-7 have the same stale claim. Fix: reword (e.g., \"B2 exists as yin.vm.debruijn-linearize; this kernel still doesn't consume it — eval by composition/lift is out of scope for B3\").\n\nWait — is the ns docstring claim even stale at time of commit? Since B2 files are in the same worktree/commit, yes.\n\nP2-2: corpus mnemonic coverage is asserted only in prose. The test file claims all 21 mnemonics are reached but no test computes the union of first elements across adapted corpus images vs code/mnemonics. If a fixture regresses (e.g., walker change drops :park), the \"every node and opcode\" completion criterion (design's B2 box) silently fails. Fix: add `(is (= code/mnemonics (into #{} (mapcat (fn [[_ ast]] (map first (:image (adapted ast)))) corpus))))` — cheap.\n\nHmm — I did manually verify the corpus does reach all mnemonics via AST construction, and ast->datoms saturates defaults. So coverage holds today; just not enforced. P2.\n\nP3-1: fallback test vacuous (arity mismatch → ignored at lift-params, so the failing-round-trip branch in `lift` is never exercised). Suggest a fixture with matching arity that captures a free name (e.g., worked-example with params '[+] at the closure pc) that would genuinely fail round-trip and exercise the fallback.\n\nP3-2: `lift-once` throws a raw IndexOutOfBounds on scope-invalid images (nth chain depth); precondition not documented. Also `image-scope-defect` silently assumes layout-conforming (body-owner is ill-defined on overlapping bodies); docstring only mentions shape-validity.\n\nP3-3: The :push no-op creates an implicit contract for B4: every future value-producing op (:stream-*, :ffi-call, :gensym, :current-continuation, :resume) must conj its result onto :stack or the value is silently lost (no val register exists). The comment should call out this obligation for B4 explicitly.\n\n:push fix verdict: CORRECT — verified against semantic.cljc:275-277 (opcode 22, St ← St ++ [val], val accumulator distinct from St), all :push emission sites in linearize.cljc (datom lane 93, 96, 113, 120; row lane 270, 273, 288, 293 — each immediately after a lower-node whose final instruction is a producer), and every value-producing case implemented in stack.cljc (const/load-bound/load-free/closure/call (both closure and fn? paths)/store-get/store-put) conj-ing directly onto :stack. No other register holds a produced value, and unimplemented producers throw :not-yet-implemented, so the no-op cannot mask a lost value today. Also verified the related convention that :branch-false reads val without consuming St in named VM but pops in stack VM is sound because lower never emits :push after a test node.\n\nAdditional edge verified: rightmost-wins resolve-name + bind-positional nil-padding exactly matches engine/bind-params (into {} over padded pairs, last duplicate wins — including under-arity ((fn [x x] x) 5) → nil on both VMs). No parity defect here.\n\nRename verification (code): no file requires or references yin.vm.debruijn-vm as a namespace anymore; stack_test requires yin.vm.debruijn.stack and the intentionally preserved yin.vm.debruijn-vm-contract-test; old files gone (git status shows staged rename). Only the doc rename is missing (P1-1) and stale body claims (P2-1).\n\nB2 vs design's B2 box:\n- lower unchanged ✓ (linearize.cljc untouched — git status doesn't show M; not in the change list ✓)\n- resolve-name the sole projection helper reused ✓\n- scope reconstruction is pure function of image, never :source ✓ (:source carried but only for side-table)\n- innermost-first stack, explicit inversion documented ✓ (chain-of docstring)\n- closure-ranges/layout-conforms? replicated exactly (verbatim comparison with completion.cljc:132-159 ✓)\n- layout failure = validation defect ✓ (:layout ex-info; tests cover unclosed body + overlapping)\n- determinism ✓ tested\n- every node and opcode — corpus covers, but not asserted (P2-2)\n- lexical validation ✓ (well-formed-vector? + rewrite layout check, tested)\n- structural compare differing only at :var/:closure ✓ tested\n- image encode/validate/load roundtrip — hmm: \"image encode/validate/load roundtrip\". Tests: validate (well-formed-image?, image-defect) ✓; load (create-vm) ✓; ENCODE roundtrip? There's adapting-twice-is-byte-identical (image-hash determinism), but no encode-image → decode → image roundtrip. But B1 \"does not construct a decode/receive path\" (debruijn_code.cljc docstring lines 34-40) — decode doesn't exist yet, so encode roundtrip is not constructible. The design's B2 box says \"image encode/validate/load roundtrip\" — since B1 has no decoder, encode roundtrip is untestable; hash determinism is the available substitute. Note as a P3 finding? Since the decode path doesn't exist (documented in B1), B2 couldn't have implemented that criterion. Not a B2 defect — flag as an observation (criterion deferred to receive path).\n- lift law strict equality ✓ tested on 4 programs\n- synthesized is alpha-equivalent including (fn [x x] x) ✓ tested\n- synthesized fresh against free names ✓ implemented (used set) — tested indirectly through roundtrip\n- side-table only accepted if its adaptation reproduces image ✓ implemented; test weak (P3-1)\n- Every image B2 emits accepted by B1 validator ✓ tested; hand-built out-of-range rejected by both ✓ tested (and I traced agreement of both validators on both fixtures)\n\nOverall verdict: READY WITH CHANGES. P1 is orchestrator's rename step (doc), not B2's code; B2's code itself: no correctness defect found; :push fix correct.\n\nTimestamps: no clock access (shell refused). Created at 09:33:20 GMT; I'll note completion as approximate and be explicit that shell was refused so exact time unavailable. Actually the header format demands an exact stamp. Best effort: note \"(approximate; no clock access — shell_command refused in this session)\". Local timezone: caller is Indochina Time (+07).\n\nLet me write the final report. It should be thorough yet concise.\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"All files read. I traced the `:push` fix against both VMs, hand-executed the runnable corpus, verified the duplicate-parameter/under-arity edge against `engine/bind-params`, and diffed B2's layout helpers against `completion.cljc`'s privates. Here is the report.\n\n---\n\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-09-22 ~10:20 GMT (approximate — `shell_command` was permission-denied in this session, so no clock could be read; no other time source available)\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-22 ~17:20 +07 (Indochina Time, approximate, same reason)\nCoding-Agent: cmd\nSession-ID: 371434a6-5144-4a5f-b739-0af9b69baf07\n\n## Verdict: READY WITH CHANGES\n\nOne P1 (the orchestrator's rename step is incomplete), two P2s (stale claims, unenforced coverage), three P3s. **No correctness defect found in B2's code or in the `:push` fix.**\n\n## What I ran\n\nRead-only. Full reads: `debruijn_linearize.cljc`, `debruijn_linearize_test.cljc`, `debruijn/stack.cljc` (266 lines), `debruijn/stack_test.cljc` (321 lines), `docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-vm.md` (667 lines), plus supporting `debruijn_code.cljc` (852), `linearize.cljc` (447), `code.cljc`, and targeted reads of `semantic.cljc` (hot loop 180–379, incl. opcode 22), `debruijn.cljc` (`resolve-name`), `engine.cljc` (`bind-params`), `completion.cljc` (`closure-ranges`/`layout-conforms?`), `vm.cljc` (walker defaults). Repo-wide greps for the old name (2 passes). One `shell_command` (`git status`) attempted and denied by permissions; no tests, builds, or edits run.\n\n## Findings\n\n**P1-1 — The design doc rename was not performed.** `docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md` does not exist (read attempt: \"File not found\"; glob of `docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn*` returns only `-vm.md` and `-projection.md`). Yet seven files cite the nonexistent path: `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:2`, `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_linearize.cljc:2`, `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc:2`, `test/yin/vm/debruijn/stack_test.cljc:2`, `test/yin/vm/debruijn_linearize_test.cljc:2`, `test/yin/vm/debruijn_code_test.cljc:2`, `test/yin/vm/debruijn_vm_contract_test.cljc:2`. The unrenamed doc also still carries the old names internally: line 282 (\"The VM is a new `yin.vm.debruijn-vm` namespace\"), and its B3/B4/B5 boxes cite `debruijn_vm.cljc` / `debruijn_vm_test.cljc` paths (lines 389–390, 402–403, 418). Fix before commit: rename the doc, update those five internal spots, or revert the seven citations.\n\n**P2-1 — Stale \"B2 does not exist yet\" claims in the merged kernel.** `debruijn/stack.cljc` ns docstring lines 10–13 and the `eval` ex-info message (lines 249–251: \"B2 (the named-datom lowerer) does not exist yet\") — and `stack_test.cljc` lines 5–7. B2 lands in the same commit, so the runtime-visible `eval` message states a falsehood. The require claim itself (\"never requires `yin.vm.debruijn-code`\") is still true. Reword, don't delete: `eval` legitimately stays unimplemented in B3.\n\n**P2-2 — Corpus mnemonic coverage is prose-only.** `debruijn_linearize_test.cljc`'s `corpus` docstring claims all 21 `code/mnemonics` are reached (I verified by hand-construction that they are, and that `ast->datoms` saturates the gensym-`\"id\"`/buffer-`1024` defaults so `:saturation` can't fire), but no test computes the union of `(map first image)` across the adapted corpus and compares it to `code/mnemonics`. The B2 box's \"every node and opcode\" criterion can silently rot. One cheap `is` closes this.\n\n**P3-1 — The foreign-side-table fallback test is vacuous.** `a-foreign-side-table-that-fails-to-round-trip-falls-back-to-synthesis` sets `[0 :params]` to a 2-name vector for an arity-1 closure; `lift-params` ignores it on the arity check, so the first attempt already round-trips and `lift`'s failed-check fallback branch (`(lift-once v nil)` after `(= v (:debruijn (rewrite attempt)))` is false) is never executed. A same-arity capturing name (e.g. `'[+]` on worked-example, which would re-resolve `:load-free +` to `:load-bound`) genuinely fails round-trip and exercises the branch.\n\n**P3-2 — `lift` preconditions undocumented.** `lift-once` throws a raw `IndexOutOfBounds` (`(nth chain depth)`) on a scope-invalid image, and `image-scope-defect`'s `body-owner` is ill-defined if `layout-conforms?` fails (only shape-validity is disclaimed). Both are fine under \"B1's validator is the sole admitter,\" but the docstrings should say so.\n\n**P3-3 — The `:push` no-op creates an unwritten B4 obligation.** Every future value-producing opcode (`:stream-*`, `:ffi-call`, `:gensym`, `:current-continuation`, `:resume`) must `conj` its result straight onto `:stack`; a B4 implementation that parks a value anywhere else would have it silently dropped by the no-op `:push` (there is no `val` register to recover from). The comment above `:push` should name this obligation. Related observation: the B2 box's \"image **encode**/validate/load round trips\" is only partially satisfiable — B1 built no decode path (`debruijn_code.cljc` lines 34–40), so hash-determinism + validate + load is the available substitute; not a B2 defect.\n\n## `:push` fix verification (requested explicitly)\n\n**Correct.** Verified independently, not from the comment:\n- Named VM (`semantic.cljc`): opcode 22 at lines 275–277 is `St ← St ⧺ [val]`, and every producer (`:const` 1, `:var` 2, `:closure` 4, `:call` 5/20 via `apply-call`, `:store-get` 10, `:store-put` 11, etc.) writes the `val` register, never `St`. The split is real.\n- Stack VM (`debruijn/stack.cljc`): every implemented producer (`:const`, `:load-bound`, `:load-free`, `:closure`, `:call` both closure and `fn?` paths, `:store-get`, `:store-put`) `conj`s onto `:stack`. No other register can hold a produced value, so \"commit the already-pushed value\" is the only meaning `:push` can have here.\n- Every `:push` emission site in `linearize.cljc` (datom lane 93, 96, 113, 120; row lane 270, 273, 288, 293) comes immediately after a `lower-node` whose final instruction is a producer — no stale-val site exists, so no site needs move semantics.\n- Masking check: B2's `rewrite` copies `:push` tuples unchanged and never emits new ones; unimplemented producers throw `:not-yet-implemented`, so today no path can lose a value through the no-op. The merged `stack_test.cljc` fixtures contain zero `:push` instructions — no behavior change to the signed-off kernel tests.\n- Consistency spot-check: named `:branch-false` reads `val` without touching `St` (line 282) while the stack version pops — sound because `lower` never emits `:push` after a test node.\n\nI also hand-executed all five runnable corpus programs (`:literal`, `:duplicate-param`, `:worked-example`, `:zero-arity-call`, `:if-in-tail`) through both machines' transition rules; results agree (e.g. worked-example = 11, if-in-tail = 2). And I checked the sharpest parity edge I could find — under-arity call with duplicate params, `((fn [x x] x) 5)`: `resolve-name` gives `[0 1]`, `bind-positional` gives frame `[5 nil]` → `nil`; named `bind-params` = `(into {} (map vector [x x] [5 nil ...]))` → last duplicate wins → `{x nil}` → `nil`. They match, including the nil-fill case.\n\n## Rename verification (code side)\n\nClean apart from P1-1/P2-1: repo-wide grep finds no require, ns form, or code reference to `yin.vm.debr"}]}}
