nchanged and never emits new ones; unimplemented producers throw `:not-yet-implemented`, so today no path can lose a value through the no-op. The merged `stack_test.cljc` fixtures contain zero `:push` instructions — no behavior change to the signed-off kernel tests.\n- Consistency spot-check: named `:branch-false` reads `val` without touching `St` (line 282) while the stack version pops — sound because `lower` never emits `:push` after a test node.\n\nI also hand-executed all five runnable corpus programs (`:literal`, `:duplicate-param`, `:worked-example`, `:zero-arity-call`, `:if-in-tail`) through both machines' transition rules; results agree (e.g. worked-example = 11, if-in-tail = 2). And I checked the sharpest parity edge I could find — under-arity call with duplicate params, `((fn [x x] x) 5)`: `resolve-name` gives `[0 1]`, `bind-positional` gives frame `[5 nil]` → `nil`; named `bind-params` = `(into {} (map vector [x x] [5 nil ...]))` → last duplicate wins → `{x nil}` → `nil`. They match, including the nil-fill case.\n\n## Rename verification (code side)\n\nClean apart from P1-1/P2-1: repo-wide grep finds no require, ns form, or code reference to `yin.vm.debruijn-vm` as a namespace anywhere in `src/`/`test/` (only the deliberately-kept `yin.vm.debruijn-vm-contract-test`, the stale doc, collab prompts, and the historical orchestrator log). `stack_test.cljc` requires `yin.vm.debruijn.stack` and `yin.vm.debruijn-vm-contract-test`, both of which exist. Old files are gone (staged renames). The coexistence of `debruijn.cljc` (dormant projection) and the new `debruijn/` directory is legal for require resolution on all three hosts.\n\n## B2 vs the design's B2 box\n\n`lower` unmodified ✓; `resolve-name` the only projection helper reused ✓; scope reconstruction pure over the image, `:source` never read back ✓; innermost-first chain with the explicit-opposite-order conversion documented ✓; `closure-ranges`/`layout-conforms?` reproduced verbatim from `completion.cljc:132–