tack VM, `:call` conj's the result onto the stack. So `:push` after `:call` also becomes a no-op. So what about `:store-put`? In the stack VM it conj's the value. In the named VM, `:store-put` probably puts the value into `val`, and a subsequent `:push` commits it. OK.\n\nBut is there anywhere in the named VM where `:push` is emitted without the immediately preceding producing instruction having been conj-ed? I need to check linearize's lowering to see where `:push` gets emitted. Let's read linearize.cljc.\n\nAnother important point: the stack VM's `:return` pops… actually `:return` peeks the stack and truncates down to stack-base. And `:call` reads operands from the top of the stack. Since `:push` is a no-op and producers directly conj, the stack discipline is preserved.\n\nPotential issue: what if linearize emits `:push` after something like `:branch-false`? I need to read the lowering code.\n\nFurthermore, let's read sections 1–3 of the design document and the B2 box, and additionally check the semantics of `yin.vm.debruijn/resolve-name`, `yin.vm.code/vector-operand-table`, `well-formed-vector?`, `well-formed-image?`, and `scope-defect` to verify the B2 logic.\n\nLet's read these files.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now the design doc and the supporting namespaces B2 depends on.\n\n"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_ba989bc02bcd4bb9ba9935f0","name":"read_file","input":{"file_path":"/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-debruijn-b2/docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md"}}],"meta":{"source":"model","createdAt":1790067227193,"messageId":"45bde37d-78a5-47c1-a675-27bea6b30ca2"}},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_ba989bc02bcd4bb9ba9935f0","content":[{"type":"text","text":"File not found or not readable: /Users/sto/workspace/worktree-debruijn-b2/docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md"}]}],"meta":{"source":"tool","messageId":"eaa6f295-4253-40cf-930e-9f0a9a6f4789"}},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The documentat